"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000 (later adjusted to $550,000 for real-time analytics integration). Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and a prototype for secure file sharing ahead of schedule. The project has established a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research and is expanding the team with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. The project is moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with UI enhancements planned for October. A celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and security protocols (MFA and encryption) will be updated effective January next year. The project is currently on track for final delivery."
